            "body": "is there a more low-level approach? we really just need the existing message:\r\n\r\n    E5108: Lua: [string \":lua\"]:1: bad argument #1 to 'pairs' (table expected, got userdata)\r\n\r\nto change to:\r\n\r\n    E5108: Lua: [string \":lua\"]:1: bad argument #1 to 'pairs' (table expected, got vim.NIL)\r\n\r\nand i would expect there's some way in C to change the \"tostring\" form of `vim.NIL` so that it reports `vim.NIL` instead of `vim.NIL`",
